# Nginx Proxy Manager SSL

## Gate

Use when the user authorized NPM work and the turn needs **SSL certificate**
list, issue, renew, or attach-to-host. Host structure without cert work →
`nginx-proxy-manager-hosts`. Delete cert / bulk renew → also
`nginx-proxy-manager-safety`.

## Transport

No NPM MCP discovered. Prefer REST API on an operator-resolved `BASE` with
Bearer auth (see hosts rule), or admin UI. **Do not invent MCP tool names.**
Never paste private keys, CF tokens used for DNS challenge, or admin
passwords into chat — reference secret **names** or “token already on NPM
settings” only.

## API map (HTTP)

| Need | Method + path |
| --- | --- |
| List certificates | `GET /api/nginx/certificates` |
| One certificate | `GET /api/nginx/certificates/{id}` |
| Request / upload cert | `POST /api/nginx/certificates` (provider-specific body) |
| Delete certificate | `DELETE /api/nginx/certificates/{id}` (safety gate) |

Attach a cert to a proxy host by updating the host (`certificate_id` /
SSL fields) via `nginx-proxy-manager-hosts` after the cert id is resolved.

## Providers (craft language)

| Provider shape | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP-01 (standard Let’s Encrypt) | Domain must already point at NPM; wait for DNS |
| DNS-01 | Needs a DNS plugin/credential **already configured in NPM** — do not dump provider API tokens into chat |
| Custom / upload | User supplies cert material through UI/API upload channels they control — do not paste PEM private keys into the agent chat |

Confirm provider enum values from a live list/get or NPM docs for that
version — do not invent provider strings.

## Discover first

1. Never invent certificate ids — list/resolve this turn.
2. Before renew/delete, `GET` the cert and show domain names + expiry /
   provider from evidence.
3. Before attaching to a host, prove the host id and cert id both exist.

## Craft defaults

1. Prefer renew / re-issue on the **same cert id** when the product supports
   it over delete+create.
2. Multi-SAN certs: list every domain in the receipt.
3. Do not force-renew unrelated certs in bulk without named ids
   (`nginx-proxy-manager-safety`).
4. After issue, optionally show which proxy hosts reference `certificate_id`
   (from host list filter) — do not guess.

## Report shape

- **id**
- **domain_names** (SANs)
- **provider** / nice name
- **expires_on** when present
- **attached hosts** (ids/domains) when known from host inventory

## Refuse

- Pasting private keys, intermediate PEMs, or DNS provider API tokens
- Inventing cert ids or claiming LE success without API/UI evidence
- Deleting a cert still attached to enabled hosts without an explicit delete
  verb naming the cert **and** acknowledgment of attached hosts

## Related (this plugin)

- `nginx-proxy-manager-hosts` — attach cert id on proxy host
- `nginx-proxy-manager-safety` — delete / bulk renew gates
